# NOTE ON ORDERING: in .gitattributes the LAST matching line wins -- the opposite of
# .gitignore intuition. The general rule must therefore come FIRST and the specific
# overrides after it. Getting this backwards silently re-enabled newline translation on
# the hashed artifacts and made `sha256sum -c` fail on a fresh clone.

* text=auto

# Hashed artifacts must survive checkout byte-for-byte.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf enabled, so git would otherwise
# rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout. For the frozen splits that is fatal: the bytes change,
# `sha256sum -c splits.sha256` fails on a clean clone, and the benchmark looks tampered
# with. `-text` disables all newline translation for these paths.
benchmark/splits/** -text

# Fixtures are compared byte-wise by the test suite for the same reason.
src/ecopulse_ca/ingest/fixtures/*.json -text
